  "narrative": "The first-pass results are dominated by three main effects. Estimates are signed to the claimed direction, which is -1 for these main claims; positive signed values indicate the expected direction (raw negative, stronger dependency), while negative signed values indicate the opposite raw direction. H5 (SMARCA4 loss) is accepted because its signed estimate +0.833 has a 95% interval [+0.767, +0.908], entirely above the 0.15 threshold and entirely on the claimed side. This is a very large association in the supplied dataset: SMARCA4 loss corresponds to a substantially more negative composite dependency score, i.e. stronger dependency. By contrast, H2 (TP53 loss) and H4 (KEAP1 loss) are rejected for the pre-registered negative-direction claims: their signed estimates are large negative values, meaning the raw exposed-minus-comparator contrasts are positive (weaker dependency) and very precise. These are not marginal reversals; they exceed the threshold in the opposite direction. The remaining main-effect claims are rejected because their claimed-direction intervals are either near zero or well below the 0.15 threshold: KRAS, STK11 loss, MYC amplification, research markers D/E, and the Avana library indicator do not support the claimed stronger-dependency associations. The pre-registered interactions also fail: the KRAS effect does not differ meaningfully by adenocarcinoma subtype, the KEAP1 effect does not differ meaningfully by STK11-loss background, and the research-marker-D effect does not differ meaningfully across high versus low research signature B. Given the strength and interpretive importance of the SMARCA4 result, I request independent validation of H5. I also register reversed TP53 and KEAP1 claims because the data strongly suggest opposite associations, and register co-mutation-restricted context analyses to check whether SMARCA4 and TP53/KEAP1 associations persist after controlling for major co-altered backgrounds. These refinements address possible confounding by correlated genetic alterations. Causality and broader generalizability remain unestablished.",
  "research_notes": "First-pass conclusions: accepted in this dataset: SMARCA4 loss associated with much stronger dependency (raw contrast about -0.83). Rejected pre-registered negative claims but observed robust opposite raw associations: TP53 loss and KEAP1 loss are associated with less negative dependency scores, i.e. weaker dependency. Other first-pass predictors and technical marker/library variables show no meaningful association, and pre-specified interactions are null. Validation requested for H5. Next priorities: (1) test reversed TP53/KEAP1 direction +1 claims; (2) test SMARCA4 effect restricted to KEAP1/STK11 wildtype and reversed KEAP1/TP53 effects restricted to other co-mutation wildtype backgrounds; (3) add research_marker_f main effect. If reversed claims remain strong in context-restricted analyses, treat them as dataset-specific association findings; if context analyses weaken them, favor co-mutation confounding. Do not overinterpret lineage subtype interactions: dataset is single lung lineage and only adenocarcinoma vs complement; H10 showed no meaningful KRAS subtype interaction.",
  "validate": "H5"
